    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0859" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51/1–845</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by The Secretary of State to President
                        Roosevelt </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-08">January 8, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>When we talked together on the 23rd of December, I referred briefly to the
                    attached memorandum<anchor n="13" xml:id="d832-f1"/> outlining a program of
                    seeking Congressional approval for direct financial aid to Saudi Arabia.</p>
                <p>Lend-Lease aid will not be available for this purpose after this fiscal year. The
                    attached memorandum gives reasons indicating why it is in our national interest
                    to extend this assistance, otherwise Saudi Arabia will undoubtedly turn
                    elsewhere with resulting grave long range effects on our position in that
                    country. The War and Navy Departments agree as to its desirability. Estimates of
                    the amount involved vary from a minimum of 28 million to a maximum of 57
                    million, for the five year period 1945–50.</p>
                <p>We did not have the time to go into the matter thoroughly together but it was my
                    understanding that you were favorably inclined towards the proposal. I enclose
                    the memorandum from which we talked for your consideration and approval.<anchor
                        n="14" xml:id="d832-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius, Jr</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
